 "title": "Mastering Communication Pace",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator explains that effective communication is not just about speaking clearly, but also about mastering your speaking tempo. The main lesson is to learn when to slow down and when to speed up to keep people listening.",
 "key_points": [
  "Communication is not just about speaking clearly or using the right words.",
  "People may not listen to you if you don't know when to slow down and when to speed up.",
  "Observe how speakers vary their speed between fast and slow to maintain engagement."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by CS. Balgopal Sridharan | Teacher. Text / caption: Comment “SPEAK” to get your communication audited. Transcript: See, that's funny because you actually expect these people to believe that I never went to law school at all and yet still somehow manage to convince the smartest lawyers in the world to make me their youngest partner ever. Many people think communication is about speaking clearly, but that's not true. You can speak clearly, use all right words, and still people may not listen to you. You know why? Because you don't know when to slow down and when to speed up. That's why in today's video we are going to learn about. Text on screen: Observe how Mike switches between fast & slow. Comment “SPEAK” to get your communication audited",
